The changes PetriScan's build makes to Microsoft's ONNX Runtime source, applied
by .github/workflows/build.yml (README.md).

env.h: Windows' environment keeps ONNX Runtime's no-op telemetry, the Telemetry
base class its Linux and macOS builds use, rather than WindowsTelemetry. So the
library never registers the Microsoft.ML.ONNXRuntime provider
{3a26b1ff-7484-7484-7484-15261f42614d}, which Windows' diagnostic data listener
subscribes to by its ID, and no telemetry event can be written. Everything
reaches the member through the Telemetry interface (GetTelemetryProvider), so
nothing else changes, and inference is untouched.

onnxruntime.rc: the version information says the library is PetriScan's build,
since Microsoft neither built nor signed it. The copyright stays Microsoft's.

diff --git a/onnxruntime/core/platform/windows/env.h b/onnxruntime/core/platform/windows/env.h
index df8a3e1..712b79b 100644
--- a/onnxruntime/core/platform/windows/env.h
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/platform/windows/env.h
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@ class WindowsEnv : public Env {
  private:
   void InitializeCpuInfo();
   typedef VOID(WINAPI* FnGetSystemTimePreciseAsFileTime)(LPFILETIME);
-  WindowsTelemetry telemetry_provider_;
+  Telemetry telemetry_provider_;
 };
 
 namespace internal {
